hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15385","Haddathana Hushaym ibn Bashir, from Abu Bishr Ja'far ibn Iyas, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man comes to me asking for a sale I do not have to sell, then I sell it from the market. He said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"15386","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, haddathana Shu'bah, from Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, relating from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not to fall except standing. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man asks me for a sale and I do not have it; shall I sell it to him? He said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"15387","Haddathana Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, Ayyub informed us, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to sell what I do not have. Ayyub said: Or he said: goods I do not have."
"15388","Haddathana Isma'il, haddathana Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith al-Hashimi, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders have the choice as long as they have not parted; if they are truthful and clarify, their sale is blessed with provision, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped out."
"15389","Haddathana Yahya ibn Adam, from Shu'bah, haddathana Abu Bishr, from Yusuf ibn Mahak, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, goods are sought from me and I do not have them; shall I sell them to him? He said: Do not sell what you do not have."
"15390","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, haddathana Hisham, meaning al-Dastuwai, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir related to me, from a man, that Yusuf ibn Mahak informed him that Abd Allah ibn Ismah informed him that Hakim ibn Hizam informed him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I buy sales; what of them is lawful for me and what is forbidden to me? He said: When you buy a sale, do not sell it until you take possession of it."
"15391","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Amr ibn Uthman, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is from surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"15392","Haddathana Abd al-Razzaq, haddathana Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about matters I used to devote myself with in ignorance, of freeing slaves and joining kinship: is there reward for me in them? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You embraced Islam with the prior good you sent forth."
"15393","Haddathana Uthman ibn Umar, Yunus informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, that Hakim ibn Hizam informed him, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about matters I used to devote myself with in ignorance? He said: You embraced Islam with the prior good you sent forth. And devotion is worship."
"15394","Haddathana Abd Allah, he said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Haddathana Sa'id, meaning Ibn Sulayman, haddathana Abbad, meaning Ibn al-Awwam, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Ayyub ibn Bashir al-Ansari, from Hakim ibn Hizam, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about charities, which of them is best? He said: Upon the hostile relative."
"15395","Haddathana Yazid, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for wealth and I persisted, and he said: O Hakim, how much you ask, O Hakim; this wealth is green and sweet, and with that it is only the filth of people's hands; and the hand of Allah is above the hand of the giver, and the hand of the giver is above the hand of the receiver, and the lowest of hands is the hand of the receiver."
"15396","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Hammad ibn Salamah, Qatadah informed us, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from Hakim ibn Hizam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders have the choice as long as they have not parted; if they are truthful and clarify, their sale is blessed, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped out."
"15397","Haddathana Attab ibn Ziyad, haddathana Abd Allah, meaning Ibn Mubarak: Layth ibn Sa'd informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mughirah related to me, from Irak ibn Malik, that Hakim ibn Hizam said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most beloved man among people to me in ignorance; when he became a prophet and went out to Madinah, Hakim ibn Hizam attended the season while a disbeliever, and found a suit of Dhu Yazan offered for sale, so he bought it for fifty dinars to gift it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He brought it to him in Madinah and urged him to accept it as a gift, but he refused. Ubayd Allah said: I thought he said: We do not accept anything from the idolaters; but if you wish, we take it for a price. So I gave it to him when he refused the gift from me."
"15398","Haddathana Affan, haddathana Hammam, haddathana Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders have the choice as long as they have not parted. He said: I found in my father's book: the choice three times; if they are truthful and clarify, they may gain profit, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped out."
"15399","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Ja'far, haddathana Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Salih Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two traders have the choice as long as they have not parted; if they are truthful and clarify, their sale is blessed, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their sale is wiped out."
"15400","Haddathana Waki', he said: I heard Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support; whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will suffice him, and whoever seeks chastity, Allah will make him chaste."
"15401","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, both of them said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, Ibn Jafar said in his hadith, he said: I heard Abu al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Hakim ibn Hizam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The two traders have the choice as long as they have not parted. He said: If they are truthful and make things clear, their transaction will be blessed for them, and if they lie and conceal, the blessing of their transaction will be wiped out. And Ibn Jafar said: wiped out."
"15402","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, from the same, he said: as long as they have not parted."
"15403","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ata informed me that Safwan ibn Mawhab informed him, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Has there not come to me, or has it not reached me, or as Allah willed of that, that you sell food? He said: Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then do not sell food until you buy it and take full possession of it."
"15404","Ata said: Abd Allah ibn Ismah al-Jushami also informed me that he heard Hakim ibn Hizam narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
